ces", "p": ["Two cakes are the same size. One is cut into **3** equal slices, the other into **8**.", "Would you rather have 1/3 or 1/8 of a cake? Think before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Fraction names", "p": ["1/3 is one third."], "qq": {"id": "m3u11s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many eighths make a whole?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 8, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "8."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Unit fractions", "p": ["The **more** equal parts a whole is cut into, the **smaller** each part. So **1/3 > 1/8** – pick 1/3!"], "table": {"head": ["Order (smallest → largest)", ""], "rows": [["1/10, 1/8, 1/5, 1/4, 1/3, 1/2", "bigger bottom number → smaller piece"]]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Same denominator", "p": ["When the bottom numbers are the **same**, compare the top numbers: **2/5 < 4/5**.", "Order 3/7, 1/7, 6/7 → 1/7, 3/7, 6/7."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Unit", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m3u11s2t02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Bigger: 1/4 or 1/6?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "1/4", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "1/6", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I compare fractions?", "p": ["Step 1: Unit fractions: bigger bottom → smaller.", "Step 2: Same bottom: bigger top → bigger.", "Step 3: Draw bars of the same size to check.", "Step 4: Use < and >."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Unit", "p": [], "q": "1/5 or 1/2?", "steps": [["halves are bigger pieces", ""]], "a": "1/2 > 1/5"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Same bottom", "p": [], "q": "3/8 or 5/8?", "steps": [["5 > 3", ""]], "a": "5/8"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Order", "p": [], "q": "1/3, 1/10, 1/4 from smallest.", "steps": [["10 parts smallest", ""]], "a": "1/10, 1/4, 1/3"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Order same bottom", "p": [], "q": "4/6, 1/6, 5/6 from largest.", "steps": [["5, 4, 1", ""]], "a": "5/6, 4/6, 1/6"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Same bottom", "p": [], 